        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Florida Atlantic University, Cleveland State University, Charles E. Schmidt College of Science, Fenn College\n- Places: Boca Raton, Dania Beach, Davie, Fort Lauderdale, Jupiter, Fort Pierce, Cleveland, Ohio, Perry, Harbor Branch Oceanographic Institution\n- People: Cecil V. Thomas\n- Topics: public universities, academic colleges, university leadership\n\nFacts:\n- Cecil V. Thomas was born on September 17, 1892, in Perry, Ohio.\n- Cecil V. Thomas was an American educator and administrator who became the first president of Fenn College.\n- Cecil V. Thomas died on November 28, 1947, in Cleveland, Ohio.\n- Florida Atlantic University is a public university in Boca Raton, Florida.\n- Florida Atlantic University is also referred to as FAU or Florida Atlantic.\n- Florida Atlantic University has five satellite campuses in Dania Beach, Davie, Fort Lauderdale, Jupiter, and Fort Pierce at the Harbor Branch Oceanographic Institution.\n- Cleveland State University, also known as Cleveland State or CSU, is a public university in downtown Cleveland, Ohio, United States.\n- The Charles E. Schmidt College of Science is an academic college of Florida Atlantic University in Boca Raton, Florida, United States.",
